CORE
time1.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] always \$bits\(\$time\(\)\) == 64: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] always \$bits\(\$stime\(\)\) == 32: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p2\] always \$time\(\) == 0: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
$time and $stime type-check (1800-2017 20.3.1, 20.3.3). $bits gives
the width of the result. As EBMC has no notion of continuous
simulation time, the value of $time is nondeterministic, and hence the
property fixing it to 0 is refuted.
